{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/sample/pricing.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:22:28.235055Z","id":"98856668f49e7a50b707766b19209ce34f04b7e190a37a7e93e6bfb1c9ff4cb7","body":{"detail":"Two tables of the same list prices (the app agent's, in Dart, and sample()'s, in Rust) can drift; a model missing here is priced as the dearest card, so a drift errs on charging the cap early, never late. claude-haiku-4-5 is listed here only (the [sample.models] quick default) at $1/$5 per million tokens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"3d57736edb13dec2ae8099cc3372a80ab6406fe8ceae88cc5b808f5347bc8120"},"summary":"The daemon's price cards copy apps/clax_app/lib/agent/pricing.dart by hand","tags":["risk:cost","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/flight.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:57:46.223271Z","id":"15015479061497250f8de3e9637cf5024a946b07d91d6526d1c66b154160ea8f","body":{"detail":"ReaderGuard::drop calls AbortHandle::abort() and nothing else. Abort is asynchronous: the drive future, and with it Finish (whose on_finish calls AnswerCache::end, crates/clax-server/src/routes/sample.rs:211-220), is dropped only when the runtime next handles the task. Until then AnswerCache::flight (crates/clax-sample/src/cache.rs:51-58) still answers the flight, because it is not is_finished(). A second sample() call with the same cache key in that window (a page reloaded right after its tab closed, or two tabs) takes the follower branch at crates/clax-server/src/routes/sample.rs:184-191 and calls Flight::reader(). That reader sees no new frame and finished == false, and awaits notify forever, because the aborted run never pushes Done or Error. Its SSE stream stays open with no done or error frame until the browser drops it. The same happens when a reader attaches between the last guard's fetch_sub returning 1 and the abort, since readers is checked and abort taken without a lock that reader() also takes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"fc41fa717bab38099bde3ba9c317ab70e455ca2474c605f02acf865c1405e137"},"suggested_fix":"When the guard aborts, also end the flight: push Out::Error { code: \"aborted\", ... } (or set finished and call notify_waiters), so AnswerCache::flight filters it out and any reader already attached ends at once. Add a test that attaches a reader after the last one leaves and expects it to end.","summary":"A flight aborted by its last reader leaving gets no ending frame, so an identical call that follows it in the window before the aborted task drops hangs with no done or error","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/quota.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:57:46.223341Z","id":"96711b2f3d4af8870421962a0b83a190041103746c5cafee3557011e6fd43f7c","body":{"detail":"two_run_four_wait_and_the_rest_are_refused sleeps 20 ms so that four spawned waiters will have queued, then asserts the fifth enter() is refused (line 124-125). It drops a permit, sleeps 20 ms and asserts a waiter has finished (lines 127-129). a_waiter_that_gives_up_frees_its_place sleeps three times (lines 146, 148, 151). If a waiter has not run yet when the sleep ends, the fifth enter() gets a waiting place and blocks rather than being refused, and the 'a waiter finished' assertion fails. AGENTS.md ('Tests are fast and load-tolerant: no sleeps standing in for a condition') forbids this pattern. flight.rs:361 does the same to order a push after two readers subscribe.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"b915a5cf0d66d6c17bda7ac1d5bfcb391ad2d521fb1ee1bfa0efbce20b8054b7"},"suggested_fix":"Expose the waiting count (or a test hook), and loop with tokio::task::yield_now until it reaches WAITING_PER_VIEWER, rather than sleeping. Or run the tests under #[tokio::test(start_paused = true)] with explicit yields. Await the released waiter's JoinHandle, under a timeout, instead of checking is_finished after a sleep.","summary":"The viewer-queue tests wait 20 ms sleeps for conditions instead of awaiting them, and assert progress after a sleep","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/anthropic.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:57:46.223547Z","id":"1feff85542fec160c6cbcfd746beccb76f58f57f85af79efd20b370b86b66290","body":{"detail":"The Messages API also answers stop_reason \"model_context_window_exceeded\" (the answer stopped because the context window filled) and \"pause_turn\" (https://docs.claude.com/en/api/handling-stop-reasons). Both become Stop::EndTurn here. In crates/clax-sample/src/flight.rs:245-307 a context-window stop then yields Done with truncated: false. For sample.json, the cut-off text goes to json_reply::parse rather than failing with invalid_json, as a MaxTokens stop does at flight.rs:315-322.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":154},"end":{"line":161},"content_hash":"376a8da6c7c199fd301bd3aeeab92fc6597efe435fa6dff64be8bde1fac482c2"},"suggested_fix":"Map \"model_context_window_exceeded\" to Stop::MaxTokens, so the page sees truncated: true and a JSON call fails clearly. Log an unknown stop reason rather than reading it silently as EndTurn.","summary":"stop_from turns every stop reason but max_tokens, tool_use and refusal into EndTurn, so an answer cut off by the context window reads as complete","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/flight.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:30.507133Z","id":"3206c14309580634ffd4189c419deea1bf1b2c4b399e3736b645a3213d9dc0ff","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-sample/src/flight.rs:128-136: ReaderGuard::drop only takes the abort handle and calls h.abort(); it pushes no Out frame and never sets finished. clax_rt::AbortHandle is tokio::task::AbortHandle (crates/clax-rt/src/lib.rs:50), whose abort only schedules cancellation, so drive() and its Finish guard (flight.rs:150-154, which runs on_finish -> AnswerCache::end at crates/clax-server/src/routes/sample.rs:213-220) drop later. Meanwhile AnswerCache::flight (crates/clax-sample/src/cache.rs:51-58) filters only on is_finished(), so sample.rs:184-191 hands the same flight to a new reader. That reader's loop (flight.rs:103-121) finds no frame at `next`, finished false, and awaits notify; with the abort handle already taken (flight.rs:132 take()), nothing ever pushes or notifies again. stream_response (sample.rs:121-143) adds SSE keep-alives on the daemon, so the stream stays open rather than timing out. The readers fetch_sub (flight.rs:130) and reader()'s fetch_add (flight.rs:100) share no lock, so the second window the finding names exists too. Kind concern is right: a rare race, no merge-blocking failure.","kind":"comment","references":"15015479061497250f8de3e9637cf5024a946b07d91d6526d1c66b154160ea8f","summary":"confirmed: an aborted flight stays followable with no ending frame, so a follower attached before the task drops waits forever","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/quota.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:30.507304Z","id":"e512df30df42c166f6b1d5ddd638ef9f2fae24132a2d89620dec892073e2f7a3","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-sample/src/quota.rs:124, 128, 146, 148, 151 call tokio::time::sleep(20 ms) before asserting a queue state (lines 125, 129, 152-155); crates/clax-sample/src/flight.rs:361 sleeps 20 ms before pushing Done. AGENTS.md ('Code': 'no sleeps standing in for a condition') forbids this. One qualification on the failure mode: these are plain #[tokio::test] functions, which run on tokio's current_thread runtime (https://docs.rs/tokio/latest/tokio/attr.test.html), so the spawned waiters are polled when the test task yields at the sleep, before the timer can fire; the flake the finding describes is unlikely in practice on that runtime, and flight.rs:361's ordering is not needed for correctness since readers replay frames from the start (flight.rs:108-115). The rule violation stands, and concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"96711b2f3d4af8870421962a0b83a190041103746c5cafee3557011e6fd43f7c","summary":"confirmed: the viewer-queue tests and flight.rs's reader test use 20 ms sleeps in place of the conditions they wait for","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/anthropic.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:30.507896Z","id":"7cf83b1be5adbb4a627d90120f2d8680671e549c7980c9c3d4a9561721facc4e","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-sample/src/anthropic.rs:154-161 maps only max_tokens, tool_use and refusal; `_ => Stop::EndTurn`. crates/clax-sample/src/provider.rs:101-106 Stop has no other variant. crates/clax-sample/src/flight.rs:250-253 sets truncated only on Stop::MaxTokens and line 306 breaks on EndTurn, so Done carries truncated: false; flight.rs:315-322 gives the clear invalid_json 'cut short' error only when truncated, else the cut-off text goes to json_reply::parse (flight.rs:323). model_context_window_exceeded and pause_turn are documented stop reasons at https://docs.claude.com/en/api/handling-stop-reasons. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"1feff85542fec160c6cbcfd746beccb76f58f57f85af79efd20b370b86b66290","summary":"confirmed: stop_from maps model_context_window_exceeded (and every other unlisted reason) to EndTurn, so a cut-off answer is reported untruncated","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/flight.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:59:20.519007Z","id":"0313d86fb40b9d8c94d1e50088e4fee3fcca35c4f6c6000bcd6a2b53469cda73","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5e6d68913","summary":"Fixed (5e6d68913, 4c225387f, 775693312): a flight aborted by its last reader pushes an ending frame, and finished is checked and set, and read with the next frame, under the frames lock; //crates/clax-sample:clax_sample_lib_test passes (racing_ending_frames_leave_one).","supersedes":"15015479061497250f8de3e9637cf5024a946b07d91d6526d1c66b154160ea8f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/quota.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:59:20.544402Z","id":"395569393f8733afe10f0ebd7ad13d857ee5a56bc2ddabce5085888ce68c6f94","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:74a62b56f","summary":"Fixed: the viewer-queue tests poll the futures instead of sleeping; //crates/clax-sample:clax_sample_lib_test passes.","supersedes":"96711b2f3d4af8870421962a0b83a190041103746c5cafee3557011e6fd43f7c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/anthropic.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:59:20.569266Z","id":"6bfc75afe985d291dbd557788a6d0f7bcdae982602a15c92c611f6bb887d78bf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c38189e66","summary":"Fixed: stop_from reads model_context_window_exceeded as a cut-off answer; //crates/clax-sample:clax_sample_lib_test passes.","supersedes":"1feff85542fec160c6cbcfd746beccb76f58f57f85af79efd20b370b86b66290","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T23:42:41.555157Z","id":"49eebd140f31ffaafee39ad94b20f38002365745f5bd1c7f5ceb8acbcfd4c6d9","body":{"detail":"MessagesClient::stream_inner awaits bytes_stream().next() with no deadline; the native client (anthropic::client) sets only a 10 s connect timeout, and the wasm32 fetch none. A provider that stops sending mid-stream (no bytes, no close) keeps a ClaxBot turn open indefinitely. The caller can wrap the call in clax_rt::time::timeout, but the stream has no idle-gap rule of its own (for example: no event, ping included, for N seconds is a StreamCut).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":926},"end":{"line":956},"content_hash":"6f6266be6d5a46da9a405bf518317fdf94455124c6899a505ef801e460fa3377"},"suggested_fix":"Take an idle limit per call and race each next() against clax_rt::time::sleep, mapping expiry to MessagesError::StreamCut; test it with tokio's paused time.","summary":"A stalled Messages stream waits forever: no idle or total timeout on the body","tags":["claxbot","robustness","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T23:42:41.555234Z","id":"70e04e5d8b0cbf96e4d3bb466139d7a6639cc57e9ef47997b0ea974bdb835446","body":{"detail":"RetryPolicy::delay is deterministic (base * 2^n capped), so runs that hit the same 429/529 retry in lockstep. http_error (crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs:630:643) reads retry-after only as seconds; an HTTP-date value falls back to the exponential delay. Both were left out to keep the policy a pure function testable without a random source or clock.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1051},"end":{"line":1067},"content_hash":"fb1c27dca2f46441a16179f3ac47b86604d05d0599c66ab31ad130b11b47cca0"},"suggested_fix":"Add an injected jitter source (a fn(Duration) -> Duration) to RetryPolicy, and parse the HTTP-date form against an injected now.","summary":"RetryPolicy backs off without jitter, and retry-after in HTTP-date form is ignored","tags":["claxbot","retry","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T23:42:41.555278Z","id":"9592fb5c7f41cbc11925cd6e38d9a04e2af226b1ad7ad18d9c5bee754d545376","body":{"detail":"Tools are sent without eager_input_streaming, so the API validates tool input JSON before streaming it and Assembler treats input that does not parse as MessagesError::Protocol. Turning eager streaming on lets large run_script code stream as it is written, but then input can be truncated or invalid and must become an is_error tool_result instead of an error for the whole turn.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":768},"end":{"line":782},"content_hash":"5f97ab2c09985d91bba274ce5ac54ea6a6377427b309ec5979532a3add7b5fa1"},"summary":"Tool inputs stream buffered: eager_input_streaming is not offered","tags":["claxbot","revisit:run_script code is large enough that its buffered arrival shows as a visible pause in the live view","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/anthropic.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T23:42:41.555319Z","id":"91ec8fba04cb7845293e814ef9e80a1b8e4bffe20aabea8dd94dfb942e4435bd","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs has a second SSE fold (Assembler) that also keeps usage, stop_details, citations and redacted thinking. anthropic::Accumulator was left as it is so the page sample() path and its tests (crates/clax-server/tests/sample_anthropic.rs) are unchanged; the two folds now duplicate the event handling.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":176},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"69e89c2e3c9c685b82d822a9638c67ea29d01a909bace18d6a12050fc982b391"},"summary":"The sample provider keeps its own Accumulator rather than messages::Assembler","tags":["claxbot","revisit:the sample() provider needs usage or cache counts, or a fix lands in one fold and not the other","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:03:49.966314Z","id":"8f268e9bc7527625217b76b66e56553ea5af782c294a51ab29c611c9a8eae84d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:854b9c2b","summary":"MessagesClient now has Timeouts (headers, idle between body pieces, optional total), each expiring as a retryable StreamCut, through clax_rt::time::timeout on both targets. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-sample:clax_sample_lib_test --nocache_test_results --runs_per_test=30 passed 30/30 (60 tests each), including messages::tests::an_answer_that_never_comes_is_cut_at_the_header_deadline, a_stream_that_goes_quiet_is_cut_at_the_idle_deadline and pings_keep_a_stream_alive_until_the_total_cap (paused tokio time).","supersedes":"49eebd140f31ffaafee39ad94b20f38002365745f5bd1c7f5ceb8acbcfd4c6d9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:03:49.998171Z","id":"b10cfdb60d44c6ba1827c7781bc650f6d774f5c8fd7e82952c75a59ff8786a2e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:854b9c2b","summary":"Tool::eager_input_streaming (default off) now exists, and input that does not parse no longer fails the turn: it is listed in AssistantMessage::invalid_tool_inputs with the block's input set to {}. Evidence: messages::tests::input_that_does_not_parse_is_listed_for_an_error_result and betas_extra_fields_system_turns_and_eager_tools_reach_the_wire pass (bazel test //crates/clax-sample:clax_sample_lib_test, 60 passed).","supersedes":"9592fb5c7f41cbc11925cd6e38d9a04e2af226b1ad7ad18d9c5bee754d545376","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/transport.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:03:50.031160Z","id":"f772664ef287ac901ac215ba77b0d9f75581c68dc1c874c60e153dbd6875a8cb","body":{"detail":"Transport::send's wasm32 branch is checked by scripts/check-wasm.sh but no test in this repository exercises it: the clax-sample tests run natively against reqwest. Unverified at runtime: that a Worker's fetch with redirect: \"manual\" returns the 3xx itself (Reply::redirect treats status 0 as an opaque redirect too), that the retry-after header and body stream arrive, and that dropping the body stream cancels the fetch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":102},"end":{"line":158},"content_hash":"107ee3f04f56c080549eb2fe237e84c7b15a2c9b36caf2595fb1d9f95dcef558"},"suggested_fix":"Add a case to crates/clax-worker's test-wasm.mjs that points a sample or ClaxBot call at a local server answering 307 and asserts the redirect target is never called.","summary":"The wasm32 transport (fetch with redirect: manual) is compile-checked only; no test runs it","tags":["claxbot","wasm","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/anthropic.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:03:50.031276Z","id":"684b5b26b3116c4bac3337fe175088e38e37217e83bc1924c83566ff0e9e7b73","body":{"detail":"anthropic::run awaits Transport::send and each body piece with no timeout; only the page's tool waits are bounded (crates/clax-sample/src/flight.rs:294-296). A provider that stalls holds the round, its viewer's queue slot and the spawned task until the page goes away. messages::Timeouts (crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs) solves the same problem for MessagesClient and was not applied here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":272},"end":{"line":349},"content_hash":"f05eea3f35c0454c4fe22f40c8cc8a63a1c768f74ae6b71d36937ee375a2ec0a"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap the send and each bytes.next() in clax_rt::time::timeout with limits from SampleSettings, mapping expiry to ProviderErrorCode::Upstream.","summary":"The sample() provider's stream still has no deadline on its answer or between body pieces","tags":["robustness","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/transport.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:10:51.912283Z","id":"c7c19687cf968411a5d3d33ac798af362490502e10bd8a0027875a9ee03fce14","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f772664ef287ac901ac215ba77b0d9f75581c68dc1c874c60e153dbd6875a8cb","summary":"Since 4eec9b29 the wasm32 send also aborts its fetch through an AbortController when the request future or the body stream is dropped (AbortOnDrop in crates/clax-sample/src/transport.rs), so a MessagesClient deadline stops the request rather than leaving it running. Also unverified at runtime: that the Worker honours the abort signal mid-body. The suggested test-wasm.mjs case should add a stalled server and check the connection closes after the deadline.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/transport.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:17:22.421308Z","id":"8faf17da0c034b1fc5693c6cd9e7fd68f7bc55697311566700ccc2e8c0dfdec9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f772664ef287ac901ac215ba77b0d9f75581c68dc1c874c60e153dbd6875a8cb","summary":"Run at runtime by crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs under wrangler dev --local (workerd): the wasm32 transport streams three Messages turns from a scripted API on 127.0.0.1 (tool_use deltas, usage, x-api-key sent), and a cancel drops the request future mid-body, after which the scripted server sees the held connection close (check 'the cancel aborts the model request (the wasm transport's AbortController)' ok). Not covered: redirect: manual (no redirect is served), the idle and headers deadlines firing on a stalled server, and Cloudflare's own fetch.","tags":["evidence","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.208688Z","id":"f2c84a5ecd994d6be8c14c674c897bd33cfbb655a29a6d662d0a0dce7eadadcf","body":{"detail":"RetryPolicy::delay is deterministic (base * 2^n capped), so runs that hit the same 429/529 retry in lockstep. http_error (crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs:630:643) reads retry-after only as seconds; an HTTP-date value falls back to the exponential delay. Both were left out to keep the policy a pure function testable without a random source or clock.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1385},"end":{"line":1401},"content_hash":"fb1c27dca2f46441a16179f3ac47b86604d05d0599c66ab31ad130b11b47cca0"},"suggested_fix":"Add an injected jitter source (a fn(Duration) -> Duration) to RetryPolicy, and parse the HTTP-date form against an injected now.","summary":"RetryPolicy backs off without jitter, and retry-after in HTTP-date form is ignored","supersedes":"70e04e5d8b0cbf96e4d3bb466139d7a6639cc57e9ef47997b0ea974bdb835446","tags":["claxbot","retry","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-sample/src/anthropic.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.883509Z","id":"3ba8c32ccc2cf51f7b0c7e1fe3ece9d843bfaac0cc4211a9baec7a1421e0c97f","body":{"detail":"anthropic::run awaits Transport::send and each body piece with no timeout; only the page's tool waits are bounded (crates/clax-sample/src/flight.rs:294-296). A provider that stalls holds the round, its viewer's queue slot and the spawned task until the page goes away. messages::Timeouts (crates/clax-sample/src/messages.rs) solves the same problem for MessagesClient and was not applied here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":327},"end":{"line":404},"content_hash":"f05eea3f35c0454c4fe22f40c8cc8a63a1c768f74ae6b71d36937ee375a2ec0a"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap the send and each bytes.next() in clax_rt::time::timeout with limits from SampleSettings, mapping expiry to ProviderErrorCode::Upstream.","summary":"The sample() provider's stream still has no deadline on its answer or between body pieces","supersedes":"684b5b26b3116c4bac3337fe175088e38e37217e83bc1924c83566ff0e9e7b73","tags":["robustness","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
